---
description: Testing strategy & quality gates.
globs:
  - "tests/**/*.py"
  - "src/**/*.py"
---

## Purpose
Ensure correctness, prevent regressions, and keep fast feedback via unit and integration tests.

## Applies When
- Files matched by globs above under `tests/` and `src/`.

## Do
- Write `pytest` tests that cover success, edge cases, and failure paths; mock external I/O.
- Maintain high coverage on core logic (aim ≥90% on touched modules).
- Fix implementation when tests surface warnings; don’t ignore warnings.
- Keep unit tests fast; mark slow/heavy integration tests and run in nightly CI.
- Add a minimal reproducer test for each bug fix.

## Don’t
- Don’t merge with failing tests or lint.
- Don’t add brittle sleeps/timeouts; prefer deterministic checks.

## Commands / Checklist
- Run tests: `python -m pytest -q`
- Lint first: `ruff check --fix .` then `ruff format .`
- Expect 0 errors; if failures, fix tests and implementation together.
